course: dictionary
lesson: 15809
title: Uncertainty: not being sure
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Uncertainty is a noun. It means the feeling of not being sure, or something you cannot be certain about. Look for clues in the words around it. «There was uncertainty about whether the match would go ahead, because of the rain.» The words whether and because of the rain tell you that nobody knew what would happen.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Try "not being sure" instead of uncertainty: «There was not being sure about whether the match would go ahead.» It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: In science and maths, uncertainty has a special meaning: how much a measurement might be wrong. «The ruler measures to the nearest millimetre, so the length has some uncertainty.» The ruler cannot show a length more exactly than that, so the true length could be a little more or less.
fact: Uncertainty is a noun, and its plural is uncertainties.
fact: «Uncertainty» means the feeling or state of not being sure about something.
fact: «Uncertainty» can also mean something you do not know or cannot be sure about.
fact: In maths, probability describes uncertainty: an event may be certain, likely, unlikely or impossible.
fact: In science, every measurement has some uncertainty, because no measuring tool is perfectly exact.
exercise: «The family felt uncertainty about the future after the move.» What does uncertainty mean here? | A large, empty room | *Not knowing or being sure what will happen | Feeling very tired after a long walk | Being very rich
exercise: Dev says, «My ruler measures to the nearest millimetre, so my reading has some uncertainty.» What does uncertainty mean in science? | *How much a measurement might be wrong | The ruler is broken | Measuring is always easy | The number is exactly right every time
exercise: Maths uses words to describe uncertainty. Which word means an event will definitely happen? | *Certain | Unlikely | Impossible | Likely
test: «The weather forecast left everyone with uncertainty about the picnic.» What does uncertainty mean here? | A type of picnic food | *A feeling of not being sure | A happy surprise | Being very cold
test: Which word means nearly the same as uncertainty? | *Doubt | Joy | Speed | Colour
exam: Scientists write a length as «5.2 cm ± 0.1 cm» to show the uncertainty. What does the 0.1 cm show? | *The length could be a little more or less than 5.2 cm | The ruler is broken | The length is exactly 5.2 cm | The length is 0.1 cm long
